(1. Two halves, one crate) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
16 TL
T*
/F2 13 Tf
18 TL
(The core half) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
16 TL
/F1 11 Tf
(Linked into the service. It sniffs a bounded prefix, decides whether) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(it recognises the format, and parses the file into structured data.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(It is the only half that ever sees a raw byte, and it runs under the) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(read limits: no plugin may pull an unbounded file into memory.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
18 TL
(The presentation half) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
16 TL
/F1 11 Tf
(Linked into each front end. It turns that structured data into lines,) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(an icon, a picture, an edit surface, or several named views. It never) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(touches the filesystem and never sees the file itself.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
18 TL
(Why the split) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
16 TL
/F1 11 Tf
(A front end can be replaced without reimplementing eighty parsers,) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(and parsing stays off the UI thread. The service is the only process) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(that reads or writes the disk, so there is one place to audit.) Tj
T*
ET
