(2. Rules for a new plugin) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
16 TL
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(1. File the work order first. Every changed line traces back to one.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(2. State the acceptance checks. They are the definition of done, not) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   the code looking right.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(3. Land the behaviour with a test. A parser with no test is a guess.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(4. Add a fixture under samples/, and make it exercise every field) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   the plugin extracts. A hello-world proves nothing.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(5. Record the format in PLUGINS.md, built or rejected, before) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   anyone proposes it a second time.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
18 TL
(What a fixture is for) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
16 TL
/F1 11 Tf
(Two readers: a person checking the application by opening files, and) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(a test suite checking that each file still opens through the plugin) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(that owns it. A fixture too small to distinguish one plugin from) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(another serves neither.) Tj
T*
ET
